; rfc-8392 — CWT Claims Set
; DERIVED - not verbatim. RFC 8392 ships no CDDL (the string "CDDL" occurs zero
; times in it), so every rule below is this library's rendering of §2, §3,
; §3.1.1-§3.1.7, §4 Table 1 and §9.1.2, written for FX-1. Cite RFC 8392's
; prose, never this file, as the standard's own grammar.
;
; Locators are RFC 8392's. CDDL per RFC 8610.
;
; WHAT THE SOURCE FIXES AND WHAT IT LEAVES OPEN, so the choices below are
; visible rather than silent:
;   - §2 fixes the claims set as "The CBOR map that contains the claims
;     conveyed by the CWT" -> a map, not an array.
;   - §3 puts the MANDATORY claim set out of scope and §3.1 declines to make
;     any claim mandatory, so EVERY member below is optional and the empty map
;     {} is conformant. That is the source's position, not a modelling choice.
;   - §3 requires unknown claims to be IGNORED, so the extension socket is
;     wide open and failure is silent.
;   - §4 Table 1 gives the value types. §3.1.3 ALSO permits an array for aud,
;     which Table 1 and §9.1.2 both exclude; both forms appear below and the
;     disagreement is recorded, not resolved. See design-notes.md defect D-3.
;   - §9.1.1 fixes the claim-key SPACE as int / tstr of any length. Nothing in
;     the document narrows it further.

cwt-claims-set = {
  ? iss => StringOrURI            ; §3.1.1, claim key 1
  ? sub => StringOrURI            ; §3.1.2, claim key 2
  ? aud => aud-value              ; §3.1.3, claim key 3
  ? exp => NumericDate            ; §3.1.4, claim key 4
  ? nbf => NumericDate            ; §3.1.5, claim key 5
  ? iat => NumericDate            ; §3.1.6, claim key 6
  ? cti => bstr                   ; §3.1.7, claim key 7
  * other-claim-key => any        ; §3: unknown claims MUST be ignored
}

iss = 1
sub = 2
aud = 3
exp = 4
nbf = 5
iat = 6
cti = 7

; §3.1.3 against §4 Table 1 and §9.1.2. The prose admits both; the table and
; the IANA entry admit only the first. A validator generated from the registry
; REJECTS a CWT this section permits.
aud-value = StringOrURI / [+ StringOrURI]

; §2: "represented as a CBOR text string instead of a JSON text string".
; THE TYPE THAT DECIDES DEC-003: a bare COSE Key Thumbprint is a byte string
; and cannot be an iss or sub value. See design-notes.md §2.
StringOrURI = tstr

; §2: "a CBOR numeric date (from Section 2.4.1 of [RFC7049])", "modified so
; that the leading tag 1 (epoch-based date/time) MUST be omitted". §4 Table 1
; widens this to "integer or floating-point number", which is the form
; Appendix A.7 actually prints.
NumericDate = int / float

; §9.1.1's Claim Key field. The four allocation policy tiers are a REGISTRY
; policy over this space, not a type constraint, so they cannot be expressed
; here; schema/claim-key-policy.derived.yaml carries them as data with the
; CBOR encoding cost of each tier.
claim-key = int / tstr
other-claim-key = claim-key       ; any key not one of 1..7; key 0 is RESERVED

; §0 is reserved by §9.1.2 and can never carry a value.
reserved-claim-key = 0
